      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f9c7c26b9539445413970d1|full_name} This is why i mentioned that it mainly affects all users with IMU based tracking. Some examples of other usecases where this is handy might be for people with niche setups like mocap suits which dont change very much each time or those who wear their lighthouse tracked devices in the same places. Such users could simply shift the tracker around till the ingame avatar matches where it should be. Calibration is just adjusting a tracking point to a new position. You could always move your tracker to a previously calibrated position. For IMU based these positions never change. \n\nSure you can object to this but just leave the feature toggled off if this ever gets added?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
