      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "With SteamVR trackers (Vive/Tundra) it's quite easy every time to put them on the same spot and adjust their position a bit.\n\nI already do this with hip tracker. When I go to toilet, I take the the hip tracker off, then it's easier to place it on the same position as before instead of doing recalibration.\n\nThis is more noticable when using more StreamVR trackers like on elbows because it requires to do more precise T pose to calibrate them properly.\n\nAlso when VRChat crashes (that's not rare) and you are already sitting/lying, it's really annoying to get up just to recalibrate.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
